# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
# See KEYSTORE_SETUP.md for what these files are and how to (re)create them.
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
# The base64 blob that becomes the ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 repo secret, and the
# generated store/key password. Same secrecy class as the .jks itself.
**/*.jks.base64.txt
aigammon-upload.credentials.txt

# The Firebase Android config the google-services / Crashlytics / Performance
# Gradle plugins read. NOT a secret — every value in it already ships inside the
# APK — but generated, not authored: CI writes it from the AIGAMMON_FIREBASE_*
# repo variables and the FIREBASE_ANDROID_APP_ID secret, and a developer drops
# their own copy in by hand. Same tier as key.properties; committing one would
# point every fork's crash reports at this project. See firebase/DEPLOY.md.
app/google-services.json
